identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol provides an API for converting a representation back to the represented type, such as converting a numeric string to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While FoundationEssentials defines the core protocols, most implementations of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" exist in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" module.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also extends types in both ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationEssentials","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the Swift Standard Library to add formatting and parsing support."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you import "},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", you have two general approaches to perform formatting of supported types:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"code":"formatted()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"formatted(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on an instance of the type, optionally passing in a customized ","type":"text"},{"code":"FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appropriate to the type. These methods, defined by extensions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"text":", are useful for performing one-off formatting with default styles or slightly-customized styles. For example, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string123 = Double(1.23).formatted()"},{"text":" creates the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", passing in the type you want to format. This method, defined by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" itself, makes sense when you customize a style and want to format many instances with it. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string456 = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().format(4.56)"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4.56"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrangement is similar with parsing:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"code":"init(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:format:lenient:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to create instance of a type from its formatted representation. For example, to create a "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":", you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var oneTwoThree = try Double(\"1.23\", format: FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>())"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse(_:)"},{"t